Audit all repository documentation for accuracy and completeness ahead of the 0.2.0 release, and update anything stale or missing. This gates the release tag.

## Context & Scope

- Docs are organized for progressive discovery: each README is a table of contents (project `docs/README.md`, `crates/cast/docs/README.md`, `crates/cast-mcp-client/docs/README.md`).
- Verify documentation against the 0.2.0 story set merged since v0.1.0:
  - `env-var-passthrough` (PR #64)
  - `cast-local-json-overrides` (PR #65)
  - `build-repo-defined-shells` (merged to master)
  - plus anything landing from `setup-renovate` and `update-dependencies-0.2.0`
- 0.2.0 is a breaking release with no backward compatibility; docs must not reference superseded 0.1.0 behaviour. Migration-relevant changes should be surfaced for the changelog/migration notes owned by the release gate.
- Update stale entries, add missing entries for new behaviour, and confirm each README index links to entries that actually exist.
- Complete before tagging `v0.2.0`.
